# AGENTS.md

Tool-agnostic project context for AI coding agents. See `CLAUDE.md` for the same expectations described via Claude Code-specific skills/slash-commands.

## Stack

- Layout: {{LAYOUT}}
- CLI: `clap` derive subcommands
- MCP: `rmcp`, served over stdio via the `mcp` subcommand
- Release: `cargo-dist` (`dist-workspace.toml`), triggered by a human-pushed version tag — never a bot-authored commit — with changelog via `git-cliff` (`cliff.toml`); see `RELEASE.md`
- CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` gates PRs; `.github/workflows/release.yml` is generated by `dist generate` — regenerate it after editing `dist-workspace.toml`, do not hand-edit it

## Working Conventions

- Run `lefthook install` once after cloning.
- Keep transport code (CLI/MCP) thin; put real logic where it's independently testable{{CORE_CRATE_NOTE}}.
- Before a release, read `RELEASE.md`.
